const extraInsights=[
 ['agentic-architecture','Design the harness, not just the prompt','The harness is the surrounding system that supplies context, tools, state, evaluation, retries, permissions, and observability.','A strong model inside a weak harness still loops, loses state, or takes unsafe actions.','Use when moving from a demo to repeated or production work.','Do not build a platform before a simple verified loop proves the need.','Model → context assembly → tool call → state update → evaluator → bounded retry.',['pdf-agentic-10','pdf-agentic-15']],
 ['state-memory','Separate context, state, and memory','Context is what the model sees now; state is where the workflow is; memory is what should survive into later runs.','Separating them prevents a transcript from becoming an unreliable database.','Use for multi-step or resumed work.','A small single-turn task may need none of them.','Context: relevant files. State: task 3 of 7. Memory: confirmed repository convention.',['pdf-agentic-10','pdf-agentic-15','pdf-ralph-loop']],
 ['tool-design','Treat tools as typed, observable interfaces','A good agent tool has a narrow action, explicit inputs, structured output, predictable errors, and the least authority required.','Clear interfaces reduce hallucinated calls and make failures debuggable.','Use whenever Claude reaches an API, CLI, MCP, browser, or custom script.','Do not wrap a reliable CLI without a measurable benefit.','Prefer get_issue(id) over a generic shell string that can do anything.',['pdf-agentic-10','pdf-agentic-15','pdf-official-best-practices']],
 ['orchestration','Orchestrate dependencies; parallelize independence','Orchestration chooses order, ownership, handoffs, and integration across workers. Multi-agent systems help only when jobs are genuinely separable.','Explicit dependencies prevent duplicated work and conflicting writes.','Use for independent research, review, or isolated branches.','Keep tightly coupled design decisions with one owner.','Researcher → planner → writer, while independent security and test reviews fan out.',['pdf-agentic-10','pdf-agentic-15','pdf-official-best-practices']],
 ['guardrails-hitl','Put human gates at consequential boundaries','Guardrails constrain what can happen; permissions constrain authority; human-in-the-loop gates reserve irreversible judgment for a person.','Safety comes from bounded consequences, not model confidence.','Use for writes, money, secrets, deployment, deletion, or external communication.','Avoid approval prompts for harmless deterministic reads that create fatigue.','Read automatically; draft a change; require approval before push or deploy.',['pdf-agentic-10','pdf-agentic-15','pdf-official-best-practices']],
 ['evals-observability','Evaluate outcomes and trace the path','Evals measure whether tasks succeed; observability records prompts, tool calls, state transitions, cost, latency, and failures so you can explain why.','Without both, failures look random and improvements are anecdotes.','Use for repeated automation and production agents.','A one-off local edit may only need tests and a diff.','Track task success, invalid tool calls, retries, human overrides, time, and cost.',['pdf-agentic-10','pdf-agentic-15']],
 ['stopping-recovery','Define stopping, retry, and escalation conditions','Every loop needs success, failure, budget, timeout, and human-escalation exits. Reflection must compare evidence to a measurable rule.','An agent that can continue but cannot decide when to stop is an incident generator.','Use for any repeated or unattended loop.','Do not loop ambiguous creative work without review checkpoints.','Stop on verified acceptance; fail after N attempts or budget; escalate on permission or uncertainty.',['pdf-agentic-10','pdf-agentic-15','pdf-ralph-loop']],
 ['ralph-loop','Use Ralph loops only for atomic, verifiable work','A Ralph loop repeatedly selects an unfinished task, works, tests, records progress, and continues until a machine-checkable completion condition or hard stop.','Fresh iterations plus file-based state can recover from failures without carrying a decaying transcript.','Use for long tasks decomposed into single-iteration stories with reliable tests.','Avoid vague goals, unsafe host access, subjective design, or tasks without budgets.','PRD → prd.json passes flags → one story → tests → progress.txt → next iteration.',['pdf-ralph-loop']],
 ['claudemd-hierarchy','Layer CLAUDE.md at the narrowest useful scope','Global, repository, local, and nested instructions should contain only stable rules appropriate to their scope.','Scoped progressive disclosure keeps core context small while making specialized guidance available where used.','Use for monorepos, team conventions, and repeated project commands.','Do not use it as a linter, task log, or dump of every file.','Root holds shared commands; frontend/backend child files hold subsystem exceptions; personal notes stay local.',['pdf-claudemd-masterclass','pdf-official-best-practices']],
 ['hooks-enforcement','Let hooks enforce deterministic policy','CLAUDE.md explains a rule; a hook executes or blocks deterministic behavior at the correct lifecycle event.','Machines are better than prose at formatting, secret-path blocking, and required checks.','Use for stable fast checks with predictable exit status.','Avoid slow, flaky, destructive, or opaque hook actions.','Post-edit format; pre-command reject sensitive paths; stop hook verify completion.',['pdf-claudemd-masterclass','pdf-reddit-25']],
 ['knowledge-graph','Build a provenance-linked knowledge graph','A graph turns isolated documents into connected concepts; an Obsidian vault makes the map browsable by Claude Code and people.','Edges expose relationships file-by-file search misses, while source backlinks constrain hallucinated synthesis.','Use for large related document collections and recurring research.','Avoid generating hundreds of bare notes without a retrieval or review workflow.','Ingest docs → extract ideas/edges → export isolated vault → enrich notes → link each node to source → merge reversibly.',['pdf-graphify-obsidian']],
 ['daily-interface','Optimize daily interface and feedback ergonomics','Status lines, slash commands, aliases, voice input, compact output, session search, background work, and browser tools reduce coordination friction.','Small reductions in repeated interaction cost compound across many sessions.','Adopt after observing a repeated bottleneck.','Do not install every customization or patch the CLI without accepting maintenance risk.','Show branch/context status, dictate rich briefs, background long commands, and search local history.',['pdf-ykdojo-repo','pdf-reddit-25','pdf-linkedin-32']],
 ['research-writing-devops','Use Claude Code as a universal tool orchestrator—with review','Claude Code can research, write Markdown, inspect CI, drive CLIs, test browsers, create artifacts, and connect remote workflows.','The terminal provides a common interface to durable files and established tools.','Use when the task has accessible evidence and a verifiable output.','Do not treat generated research, prose, or operational changes as self-verifying.','Draft in Markdown, preserve links, investigate CI from logs/history, verify visually, then create a draft PR.',['pdf-ykdojo-repo','pdf-linkedin-32','pdf-ruben-27']]
].map(([id,title,summary,why,when,not,example,sourceIds],n)=>({id,title,summary,explanation:summary,whyItWorks:why,whenToUse:[when],whenNotToUse:[not],example,mistakes:['Using the concept without a success measure','Expanding authority before proving the loop'],advancedVariation:'Combine this concept with independent evaluation and a strict resource budget.',level:n<3?'productive':n<9?'advanced':'expert',difficulty:n<3?2:n<9?3:4,impact:9,topics:[id],sourceIds,evidenceType:'cross-source-synthesis'}));
for(const x of extraInsights)if(!insights.some(i=>i.id===x.id))insights.push(x);
